  "notes": "Widening the first drafts eye cuts made both own two pixels. A headless source-bound review was used; no interactive Lab or independent review is claimed.",
  "status": "ready",
  "rationale": {
    "legibility": "The contact-sheet 16px zoom preserves two open eye cuts and the emerging cream card; the grin is a subordinate one-pixel cue.",
    "distinctiveness": "The foreground bake-off names a jack-o-lantern card sleeve, while the plain control loses Halloween and the ghost candidate reads as chat. The neighbourhood sheet has no avoid-set collision.",
    "balance": "The target sheet keeps the card and sleeve comfortably inside circle and squircle crops, with the tilted card counterbalanced by the broad pocket.",
    "color": "Forest, pumpkin orange and neutral warm paper keep clear value separation on white, dark and grey in the contact sheet and actual Android targets.",
    "scalability": "The contact and target sheets keep the same lantern sleeve from 16px to store scale, and the exact alpha-derived Android themed icon retains its face and card.",
    "craft": "The 128px and 256px contours are clean with controlled radii, even eye cuts, a deliberate thumb notch and no spikes or stray nodes."
  },
